# Site and marketing

## Structure

- One job per section (hero → download → what it does → privacy → FAQ → releases).
- Hero budget: brand, one headline, one supporting line, one CTA group, one dominant visual idea — no stat strips or secondary promos in the first viewport.
- No cards unless they wrap a real interaction.
- Interactive burn meter is the brand demo; keep the gag consistent (`−1.2k` / `Copied −4k`).

## Brand and i18n

- Display brand: `Tokens go brrr`. Technical ids stay `tokens-go-brrr`.
- All copy through `t("key")` / `site/i18n.js` (en, fr, pt-BR). Do not hardcode English in JSX except intentional brand/provider invariants.
- Brand and provider names stay identical across locales. Lowercase via `html[data-lower]`.
- Theme: system until first click; then sticky (`tgb-theme`). Tokens in `styles.css` for light + `[data-theme="dark"]`.
- After token colour changes: `python3 scripts/check_contrast.py` (update the script's pairs too — it does not parse CSS).

## Shipping constraints

- No bundler today: React/Babel from CDN + plain JSX. Do not introduce a build step casually.
- `ds_bundle.js` is vendored; if regenerated, re-apply `window.t` patches and scrub stale `"AI usage"` kit titles.
- Releases and the site live in the one repo, `tokens-go-brrr` (GitHub Pages from `.github/workflows/pages.yml`). There is no separate releases repo.
- Keep `ABOUT.version` in `data.jsx` aligned with `pyproject.toml` when cutting site-visible releases.
